Demo Payment  card number

For a demo payment page, you can use clearly fictional card numbers. These are commonly used for testing and should not be connected to a real payment processor unless you're using that processor's official test environment.

Example demo card details:

Card Type	Demo Card Number	Expiry	CVV
Visa	4111 1111 1111 1111	12/30	123
Mastercard	5555 5555 5555 4444	12/30	123
American Express	3782 822463 10005	12/30	1234
For a pure demo website, you can also prefill the fields:

<input
    type="text"
    value="4111 1111 1111 1111"
    readonly
>

<input
    type="text"
    value="12/30"
    readonly
>

<input
    type="password"
    value="123"
    readonly
>
Or allow users to type the values while showing a hint:

<input
    type="text"
    placeholder="Demo Card: 4111 1111 1111 1111"
>
These numbers are intended for testing and demonstration only. If you later integrate a real payment gateway (such as Paystack, Flutterwave, or Stripe), use that provider's official test mode and test credentials during development rather than processing real payment details.



